node_modules/
dist/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/

# The retrieval index is COMMITTED, deliberately, and this is the note that
# stops someone re-adding it here.
#
# It is a build artifact everywhere else, and this repository is the exception
# because it is also the deployed site. Building it during the deploy would spend
# an embedding request per 32 chunks on every push — against a daily ceiling the
# readers of this site share — so it is built locally and committed instead.
# `test/docs-links.test.js` re-derives the index hash from the docs offline and
# fails when the two disagree, which is what keeps a committed index honest.
#
# A CONSUMER's project should still ignore theirs: `docs/public/rag/` there is a
# pure build artifact with no such tradeoff. `docpilot init` writes that entry.

.env
.env.local
*.log

# Repo-internal scan output, and one design note kept in Russian for its author.
CLAUDE-SECURITY-RESULTS.md
ui-specs/IDEAS.ru.md

# The Vercel CLI's local link state.
.vercel/

# Both of these are currently excluded only by the author's ~/.gitignore_global,
# so the second person to clone this repository would commit them.
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
